This kit includes material derived from Pollen Robotics' Microduck (https://github.com/pollen-robotics/microduck_rl
and https://huggingface.co/spaces/pollen-robotics/microduck-simulator), licensed under the Apache License 2.0:

- tools/skeleton.json: the robot's skeleton (bones, their placement and bind pose), from its MJCF robot description,
  scaled four times.
- bot/duck-cycles.json: walk, turn and idle cycles and one-shot moves (sit, roll, peck, kicks), recorded by running
  Pollen's trained policies in MuJoCo, with the joint data from the MJCF (base rotations, limits, default pose).
- motions/record_walk.py, make_cycles.py, record_moves.py: run Pollen's policies the way their simulator does.

Copyright Pollen Robotics. Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

Pollen's 3D meshes (CC BY-NC-SA 4.0) are not included: the bots' models are built by tools/build_bots.py. If you use
motions/build_duck.py, it reads those meshes from Pollen's repository, and the reference model it makes is an
adaptation of them, under CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 (credit Pollen Robotics, non-commercial, share alike).
